# Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io). GitHub shows a "Cite this repository"
# button from this file; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release. Two things to cite: the software
# (this record) and the corpus it publishes (preferred-citation, type dataset). Once Zenodo has issued a
# concept DOI, add it under identifiers and under preferred-citation.identifiers; do not invent one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Nuclide, please cite the dataset below and attribute it as "Data from Nuclide" with a link to
  https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide. The data are CC BY-NC 4.0. The code is MIT. Nuclide is a fork of
  OnCo (https://github.com/judegomila/OnCo); the records carried over from OnCo stay under CC BY-NC 4.0 and
  are attributed to OnCo in the files that hold them.
type: software
title: "Nuclide: a public, cited knowledge graph of radiopharmaceuticals"
abstract: >-
  Nuclide maps nuclear medicine as a linked corpus, therapy and diagnostic imaging alike: isotopes, agents,
  targets, indications, technologies, trials, companies, institutions, people, pathways, pairings, roadmaps,
  key papers, journals, bottlenecks and ideas, one record per object, each with a plain-English TL;DR, a
  technical summary, dated facts and links to primary sources. The same corpus is published as a website, a
  static JSON API with Markdown context files, Atom feeds and RDF triples, a command-line tool and a Model
  Context Protocol server. The engine and part of the corpus are forked from OnCo, a knowledge graph of
  oncology by Jude Gomila. Nothing in it is medical advice.
authors:
  - alias: casadesante
    website: https://github.com/casadesante
  - name: Nuclide contributors
    website: https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide/graphs/contributors
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide/blob/main/LICENSE
repository-code: https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide
url: https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide
keywords:
  - radiopharmaceuticals
  - theranostics
  - nuclear medicine
  - molecular imaging
  - radioligand therapy
  - medical isotopes
  - knowledge graph
  - open data
  - clinical trials
references:
  - type: software
    title: "OnCo: a public, cited knowledge graph of oncology"
    authors:
      - family-names: Gomila
        given-names: Jude
    repository-code: https://github.com/judegomila/OnCo
    license: MIT
    notes: Upstream project. Nuclide forks its engine and re-scopes part of its corpus.
preferred-citation:
  type: dataset
  title: "Nuclide corpus: radiopharmaceuticals, therapy and diagnostics"
  authors:
    - alias: casadesante
    - name: Nuclide contributors
  version: 0.1.0
  date-released: 2026-09-22
  repository-code: https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide
  license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
  license-url: https://github.com/casadesante/Nuclide/blob/main/LICENSE-DATA
  notes: >-
    Published as JSON, NDJSON, CSV, JSON Schema, Markdown context files and RDF N-Triples under /api/v1/ of
    the deployed site and attached to each tagged GitHub release. Attribution: "Data from Nuclide". Records
    carried from OnCo are attributed to OnCo in the files that hold them. Facts may be incomplete or out of
    date; verify at the primary source each record links.
